Z||000000||speed racer||04-04-2001||10:18 PM||||Can I make my V-6 sound like a ferrari if so what do I need to do it||||reg||1
Z||000001||sjp777||04-04-2001||10:30 PM||||cut off the cat and replace it with a 22" cherry bomb muffler with 2 1/4" outlets to fit over the stock pipes on either end, Not exactly a Ferrari, but much more intimidating, and all for about $20.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||04-04-2001||10:59 PM||||my turbo kit came with a special muffler. uses the stock manifolds, cat, muffler looks like a VW performance one. one inlet in center splitting and exiting both ends to each tailpipe. It sounds exactly like a real Ferrari, I have tapes of real one.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||04-05-2001||09:53 AM||||Well, tell us where you got your kit!  Can we get the muffler separately?  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||skitime||04-05-2001||10:28 AM||||I have done the cherry bomb too on two of our GTs. It is actually quieter than our third GT with Rodney Dickmans cat. I got them at Pep Boys for $14.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||04-05-2001||12:21 PM||||im sure its available somewhere seperate. look like a big 'T' cat empties into the center with the exits on both sides. sorta like 2 short cherry bombs connected in center with a pipe inlet between them. I swear Ive seen hot rod VW's with one that looks like it. It really sounds sweet wound up. I like driving with the window down just to listen to it, lol. Im sure the turbo has some to do with the sound too. Lisa and Jeremy (slammedfiero)have heard it.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 04-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||04-05-2001||12:25 PM||||I know what you mean.  I'd crank up the heat and open the sunroof just to hear my engine.  And that's with stock exhaust, but I did open up the air intake a bit.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||862M4inCA||04-05-2001||02:14 PM||||It's real simple to make your Fiero (any year or model) sound like a Ferrari.....just put a ferrari engine in.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 862M4inCA (edited 04-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||04-05-2001||06:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 862M4inCA:<BR><B>It's real simple to make your Fiero (any year or model) sound like a Ferrari.....just put a ferrari engine in.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>[This message has been edited by 862M4inCA (edited 04-05-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LMAO, well its not 'that' simple, AND NOT CHEAP, Ferrari V8 long block is $25,000 (thats not with clutch $3000, or transaxle $20,000.)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||04-05-2001||07:24 PM||||Can a cat heat shield be welded onto a cherrybomb, so nothing will look out of place at a visual inspection?<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000010||sjp777||04-05-2001||08:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>Can a cat heat shield be welded onto a cherrybomb, so nothing will look out of place at a visual inspection?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, but you probably won't pass emissions. I tried it, but barely failed. I kept the cat and got a couple 2 1/4" x 5" conector pipes from an auto parts store for about 5 bucks. I throw the cat back on for my test, then go home and put the cherry bomb back on. Works like a charm, and I can do the switch in about a half hour.||||reg||1
Z||000011||862M4inCA||04-05-2001||10:13 PM||||just tried to state the obvious Roger.....though keep in mind that I NEVER said it would be cheap....he just asked how to make his Fiero sound like a Ferrari and I gave him the most exact answer to make that so.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
